# Terraform (and the code it embeds inline, e.g. CloudFront Function heredocs)
# must check out LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites .tf to CRLF, and any
# inline code Terraform ships to a provider carries CRLF with it. That produces
# a permanent phantom diff against resources created from a LF host (CI): every
# line reads as changed while being byte-identical apart from the terminator,
# and Windows/Linux applies flip the resource back and forth forever.
# Observed on aws_cloudfront_function.forwarded_host (aws-demo).
*.tf      text eol=lf
*.tfvars  text eol=lf
*.tftpl   text eol=lf
*.hcl     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
